BDPDOBOL_02389	640513.Entas_1701	0.0	1240.0	COG0550@1|root,COG0550@2|Bacteria,1MUFZ@1224|Proteobacteria,1RN4X@1236|Gammaproteobacteria,3X1CG@547|Enterobacter	1236|Gammaproteobacteria	L	Releases the supercoiling and torsional tension of DNA, which is introduced during the DNA replication and transcription, by transiently cleaving and rejoining one strand of the DNA duplex. Introduces a single-strand break via transesterification at a target site in duplex DNA. The scissile phosphodiester is attacked by the catalytic tyrosine of the enzyme, resulting in the formation of a DNA-(5'-phosphotyrosyl)-enzyme intermediate and the expulsion of a 3'-OH DNA strand. The free DNA strand then undergoes passage around the unbroken strand, thus removing DNA supercoils. Finally, in the religation step, the DNA 3'-OH attacks the covalent intermediate to expel the active-site tyrosine and restore the DNA phosphodiester backbone	topB	GO:0003674,GO:0003824,GO:0003916,GO:0003917,GO:0006139,GO:0006259,GO:0006265,GO:0006310,GO:0006725,GO:0006807,GO:0006996,GO:0007049,GO:0007059,GO:0008150,GO:0008152,GO:0009987,GO:0016043,GO:0016853,GO:0022402,GO:0034641,GO:0043170,GO:0044237,GO:0044238,GO:0044260,GO:0046483,GO:0051276,GO:0051304,GO:0071103,GO:0071704,GO:0071840,GO:0090304,GO:0140097,GO:1901360	5.99.1.2	ko:K03169	-	-	-	-	ko00000,ko01000,ko03032	-	-	-	Topoisom_bac,Toprim
